    {
      "id": 144,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2085.5339999999997,
        4871.944000000003
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        560
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 9,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "HARD MODE, CHAINED - READ ME",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# HARD MODE, CHAINED - one script, one master, with audio\n\nWrite one prompt per shot in **Script + bindings**, separated by `---` on\nits own line (same format as the multishot workflow). Shot 1 renders in\nHARD MODE - identity from your reference images/audio - and every later\nshot continues image-to-video from the previous shot's last frame, so the\nidentity you cast in shot 1 carries down the chain in pixels. The segments\nare joined in-graph into one master with audio.\n\n- **bindings** box: your `<Picture 1>, <Picture 2> ...` identity lines.\n  They are prepended to SHOT 1 only (that's the shot that sees the refs).\n- Shot 1 length comes from the Duration node; later shots use the\n  sampler's `frames_per_shot` (243 = ~10s each).\n- Keep each shot's prompt self-contained and END each shot mid-action -\n  clean seams come from motion, not stillness.\n- The chained sampler needs at least 2 prompts; for a single shot use the\n  plain Hard Mode workflow.\n- Optional: drop a 4-step turbo LoRA into BOTH LoRA stacks at 1.0 and set\n  steps 6-8 on both stages for ~3x faster drafts (see the model page\n  description for the link). Stacks ship empty = stock quality."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
